KG42.register("rules-140240edce1dbdc0f2271ae6",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R011","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R011","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Each winning pair's local transaction price determines both the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate as kB^P + (1 - k)S^P. Scope: Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval. Condition: B^P ≥ S^P; k is predetermined in [0, 1]. Discriminatory k-DA is budget balanced: the mechanism neither financially subsidizes nor gains from transactions between buyers and sellers. Scope: Financial balance of discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller transactions.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Financial balance of discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller transactions. | Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R011-x-BP","symbol":"B^P","meaning":"Sealed bid price submitted by the winning buyer in the discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller pair; the buyer-side offer price used in the pair-specific transaction-price formula. Source scope: discriminatory k-DA settlement for a winning buyer-seller pair.","kind":"operational","domain":"Winning buyer's submitted bid price; the supplied settlement evidence states the symbol and formula but does not give a numeric domain or unit for B^P.","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R011-x-SP","symbol":"S^P","meaning":"Sealed ask price submitted by the winning seller in the discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller pair; the seller-side offer price used in the pair-specific transaction-price formula. Source scope: discriminatory k-DA settlement for a winning buyer-seller pair.","kind":"operational","domain":"Winning seller's submitted ask price; the supplied settlement evidence states the symbol and formula but does not give a numeric domain or unit for S^P.","unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R011-theta-k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Predetermined constant in the closed interval [0,1] used to weight the buyer's bid price and the seller's ask price in the discriminatory k-DA transaction-price formula; the same rate applies to the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate for a winning pair.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"[0, 1]"},"unit":"dimensionless","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Each winning pair's local transaction price determines both the buyer's payment rate and the seller's receipt rate as kB^P + (1 - k)S^P. Scope: Winning buyer-seller pairs in discriminatory k-DA local energy transactions; prices are pair-specific rather than uniform across the auction interval. Condition: B^P ≥ S^P; k is predetermined in [0, 1].","expression":"\\text{price trading buyers pay} = \\text{price trading sellers receive} = k B^P + (1-k) S^P, \\quad B^P \\geq S^P,\\ k \\in [0,1]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x-BP","v141-c-R011-x-SP"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-theta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-01","v141-b-g01-ev-03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Discriminatory k-DA is budget balanced: the mechanism neither financially subsidizes nor gains from transactions between buyers and sellers. Scope: Financial balance of discriminatory k-DA buyer-seller transactions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-09","v141-b-g01-ev-10"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-01","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"he presented in this paper. es lt u- 2.1. Review of auction mechanims er er While a multitude of mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In Discriminatory k-DA [46], otherwise known as Pay-as-Bid k-Double Auction, buyers submit sealed bid prices $B^P$ while sellers submit sealed ask prices $S^P$. Following the natural ordering rule, bid prices are sorted in a descending order while ask prices are sorted in an ascending order. If $B^P \\geq S^P$, a trade occurs at the listed price in Table 1 where $k$ is a predetermined constant in the closed interval [0, 1]. Since the trading price is determined between each winning buyer-seller pair, the described mechanism is discriminatory. A single market clearing price does not exist for each auction interval."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-03","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"a y g g p s- does not exist for each auction interval. of Uniform k-DA is a variation to discriminat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 1 Auction mechanisms. Discriminatory k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"g p all individual utilities for social welfare such that no participants are precluded from trading","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"An ideal auction mechanism encompasses four distinct properties: individual rationality (IR), budget balance (BB), incentive compatibility (IC), and economic efficiency (EE) [47]. An IR mechanism implies that no buyers/sellers shall result in negative utilities from participating in the auction. All four reviewed mechanisms exhibit IR. A BB mechanism does not financially subsidize or gain from transactions between buyers and sellers. Both VCG and TR are not BB as their market operators financially subsidize and gain from trades, respectively. IC motivates participants to bid their valuations truthfully. Both Discriminatory and Uniform k-DA do not have mechanisms to motivate truthful bidding as VCG and TR do. EE attempts to maximize the sum of all individual utilities for social welfare such that no participants are precluded from trading. Since buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are precluded from trading in TR, the mechanism, by default, does not maximize economic efficiency. While an ideal auction mechanism shall exhibit all four properties, it is important to note that the Myerson-Satterthwaite theorem [48] proves that no realistic mechanism can exhibit these four properties simultaneously."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-10","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-validation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"at o a ty, udget a a ce, a d eco o c efi c e cy out o t e ou properties; only incentive compatibilit","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 2","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Table 2 Mechanism properties. Discriminatory k-DA: IR check, BB check, EE check; Uniform k-DA: IR check, BB check, EE check; VCG: IR check, IC check, EE check; TR: IR check, IC check."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-03","quote":"Discriminatory k-DA | Price trading buyers pay: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$ | Price trading sellers receive: $kB^P + (1 - k)S^P$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-01","quote":"If $B^P \\geq S^P$, a trade occurs at the listed price in Table 1 where $k$ is a predetermined constant in the closed interval [0, 1]. Since the trading price is determined between each winning buyer-seller pair, the described mechanism is discriminatory. A single market clearing price does not exist for each auction interval."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","quote":"A BB mechanism does not financially subsidize or gain from transactions between buyers and sellers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-10","quote":"Discriminatory k-DA: IR check, BB check, EE check;"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"249455ac842b237819924125a554f477a81aed4dcb1e3d66facab56cd49561d4","applicability":"formalized","reason":"C001 is a faithful transcription of the discriminatory k-DA settlement formula: Table 1 gives the price trading buyers pay and the price trading sellers receive as kB^P + (1 - k)S^P, and the accompanying text supplies the condition B^P >= S^P with predetermined k in [0,1]. B^P and S^P are declared as operational offer-price variables from the winning pair, and k as a parameter. C002 remains not_formalized because the supplied evidence defines budget balance verbally and does not provide an explicit budget-balance equation. B evidence remains unreviewed; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-x-BP","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"B^P is the winning buyer's sealed bid price, an operational offer-price input that feeds into pricing.local and, through the pair-specific transaction price, determines the buyer's settlement payment rate. Frozen edge E001 links pricing.local to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-x-SP","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"S^P is the winning seller's sealed ask price, an operational offer-price input that feeds into pricing.local and, through the pair-specific transaction price, determines the seller's settlement receipt rate. Frozen edge E001 links pricing.local to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-theta-k","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"k is the predetermined weight in [0,1] in the discriminatory k-DA transaction-price formula. The formula is sourced at pricing.local and applied to settlement.payment via frozen edge E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"The expression is a faithful transcription of Table 1's discriminatory k-DA buyer-payment and seller-receipt rates, using the winning pair's B^P and S^P from the pricing relation and applying them at settlement.payment. Frozen edge E001 is the link between these nodes."}],"revision_requests":["B evidence remains unreviewed; source audit should confirm the unit and any numeric domain/index for B^P and S^P, because the supplied settlement quotations give the formula and condition but do not state their units or explicit numeric bounds."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
